  "summary": "Malicious code in sme-rko-finance-front-operations-overnight (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package runs a hidden dropper (_ext.js) that fingerprints the host OS/arch and downloads a platform-specific second-stage binary over HTTPS from four Cloudflare Workers origins (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If HTTPS is blocked it falls back to a DNS TXT chunked-transfer channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the Windows temp dir), chmod 755, and executed detached via /bin/sh -c or cmd.exe start /b, so it runs in the background and outlives the parent.",
